WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.881
A zebrafish brain is building its vasculature while

00:00:03.881 --> 00:00:07.313
blood is already moving through it. Some endothelial

00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:10.315
cells carry slender projections into that flow.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.264
A vessel develops under moving blood, while tiny

00:00:21.264 --> 00:00:24.125
endothelial projections meet the surrounding flow.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.935
Transparent zebrafish embryos let researchers observe

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:40.001
cranial vessels developing within a living system.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:52.138
Primary cilia can act as biological structures relevant

00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:55.654
to mechanosensing. Their distribution changes during

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:56.826
vascular development.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.593
The research combined vascular imaging with systematic

00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:10.145
assessment of endothelial cilia and hemodynamic

00:01:10.145 --> 00:01:10.737
conditions.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.308
The striking image cannot prove that each cilium

00:01:21.308 --> 00:01:24.201
measures flow. Location, developmental time and

00:01:24.201 --> 00:01:26.613
perturbation need to be distinguished.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.089
My contribution was part of a wider collaborative

00:01:35.089 --> 00:01:38.273
research programme. No single clip proves every

00:01:38.273 --> 00:01:40.547
mechanism examined in the paper.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:49.888
The useful question remains which endothelial cilia

00:01:49.888 --> 00:01:53.818
occur where, and how their distribution changes as

00:01:53.818 --> 00:01:55.291
cerebral vessels develop.
